# expand-unit-controls -- insert a CORE builtin (Test Osc) and require its EXPANDED
# control map: slot_control(M2,V/oct) (the Pitch/V-oct control) holds ONLY in the
# expanded view. From boot, plan: nav_home_to_unit_picker_dense, insert(Test Osc
# #1), expand(Test Osc #1).
#
# NOTE (honest coverage of EXPAND): a fresh insert lands the unit already EXPANDED,
# so the OFFLINE planner routes through expand to add the expanded slot_control map
# (insert itself is modeled without a slot effect), while at --run the executor
# sees expand's durable effects already hold and SKIPS driving the toggle -- the
# same idempotent-skip pattern as select_column(cv1) being a run no-op in
# seq-cv1-c3. This covers the expand operator + slot_control from a boot start
# without forcing a broken collapse-then-expand end-state. A genuine drive of
# expand (from a collapsed-unit start) composes with ui-planner-cov-starts.
focused_unit(Test Osc #1)
slot_control(M2,V/oct)
